These seven files are test data for the remote archive protocol.

Each is a "tape": a recorded conversation between a client and an
archive server. It lists requests in order and the answer a correct
server must give to each. The test in
../test_the_host_keeps_to_the_protocol.py plays each tape at the archive
host and fails if any answer differs.

They are copied, unchanged, from poslib, the library that defines the
protocol: its fixtures/remote directory at commit
b987360c6265cd53d0678b435e50c6d1cc549b37. Do not edit them here. When
pyposlib is moved to a later version of the protocol, copy them again
from the matching poslib commit and update the commit named above.
